I've exercised polearm to skilled in some games to prepare
for Ludios.  Set a bear trap in the doorway so they stick
there, be a knights jump from the spot, apply the polearm
again and again.  The only problem comes in when the first
one survives your assault long enough to escape the bear
trap and come adjacent to you - You need to switch to a
meaner melee weapon or retreat and in either case more
soldiers have time to push past the bear trap.

Ludios dragons and their mail - So far I don't recall a game
where I got silver or gray scales in Ludios.  Mean RNG
likes to taunt me with yellow or orange dragons there.

As to dealing with a zoo stealth is the way I like to go about
them.  Walk in quietly, whack monsters one by one without
waking the rest.  Not a good idea to kick in a door on the
level same as nymph avoidance strategy.  Also a good idea
to consider the monster type before killing it.  I've lost a
character in the Sokoban zoo to killing a gas spore that woke
up all the other monsters who got me before I could retreat.


